WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:08.680
Do you ever hear a noise, not a bump in the
night but a hum, a mysterious, constant and

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.889
very low frequency noise?

00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:17.640
If so, you may be one of an estimated 2% of
the global population that can hear “The

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:18.640
Hum”.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:23.310
The Hum is the name given to an ominous and
very mysterious deep-rumbling noise that can

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:26.390
reportedly be heard by thousands of individuals
across the globe.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:32.090
It apparently sounds like a very low-pitched
rumbling sound, kind of like a diesel-engine

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.350
truck idling in the distance.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:40.530
But no matter how hard people search no one
has been able to locate the source of the

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:44.570
sound, it sounds like it’s coming from all
directions equally.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:46.840
Some even say it comes from the sky.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:01:04.309
This is a recording of The Hum made in Taos,
New Mexico.

00:01:04.309 --> 00:01:07.130
For some The Hum causes headaches and nosebleeds.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:11.840
It drives others completely insane, with at
least one suicide being attributed to The

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:12.840
Hum.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.689
It’s usually heard in specific towns around
the globe for several months or years before

00:01:17.689 --> 00:01:21.590
it disappears and for some people it never
goes away.

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:26.899
The first documented occurrence of the Hum
was in Bristol in the UK, in the 1970s.

00:01:26.899 --> 00:01:32.200
A local newspaper asked Bristol city residents
“Have you heard the Hum?”

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.829
and over 800 people said they had.

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:40.349
Since then residents from hundreds of towns
and cities from all over the world have reported

00:01:40.349 --> 00:01:44.899
hearing the Hum and always describe the sound
in a similar manner.

00:01:44.899 --> 00:01:49.349
Some of the more notable locations, where
up to 12% of the population have heard the

00:01:49.349 --> 00:01:54.939
noise, are Taos - New Mexico, Largs – Scotland
and Auckland – New Zealand.

00:01:54.939 --> 00:02:00.719
Reports of the Hum have become so great that
a website has been created where people can

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:06.610
report their experience with The Hum and you
can view a map of all the reported cases.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:09.729
The Hum has even been linked to terrorism.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:16.450
In 2013 Aaron Alexis shot and killed twelve
innocent people at the Washington DC Navy

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:17.450
Yard.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:22.720
Police later found the following message on
his computer “Ultra low frequency attack

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.700
is what I’ve been subject to for the last
three months.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:30.720
And to be perfectly honest, that is what has
driven me to this.”

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:36.840
This and other evidence led conspiracy theorists
to conclude that the Hum is a government attack

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.570
or experiment being used on citizens to alter
their state of mind.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:44.810
They believe the government generates the
Hum using satellites.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:48.590
Other’s say the HAARP project in Alaska
is to blame.

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:54.960
But Illuminati and Lizard Men aside, has science
been able to find a reason for the Hum?

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.720
What is the cause?

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:01.570
Have animals learnt how to hum and are playing
a gigantic practical joke on us puny humans.

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:03.260
Is God bored?

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.120
Or is it just tinnitus?

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:11.320
The Hum is most commonly heard by people aged
between 55 and 70, so one instantly thinks

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:15.540
it’s the medical condition tinnitus, you
know how your granny is always complaining

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.490
about a ringing noise that isn’t actually
there?

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:23.710
Except for that one time you turned her hearing
aid to maximum, that was pretty bad.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:28.100
But if the cause was tinnitus shouldn’t
the spread of people who’ve reported hearing

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.319
the Hum be evenly distributed across the globe?

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:33.630
After all, tinnitus doesn’t favour certain
regions.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:40.000
But the Hum is usually reported by clusters
of people around specific locations.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.930
Also, new research carried out recently in
Cambridge, England suggests that the source

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:51.550
of the Hum is external not internal, which
is what Hum sufferers have always argued.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:56.610
People have also blamed the following things
for causing the Hum: Traffic, local factories

00:03:56.610 --> 00:04:03.570
and heavy machinery, leaking pipes, phone
masts, wind farms, submarine communication

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:10.780
systems, UFOs and even mating fish – hundreds
of Southampton residents who could hear the

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:17.130
Hum were told it was being caused by a school
of mating Midshipman fish who make this eerie

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:23.129
sound, to try to attract a female.

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:27.779
Okay that single incident with the horny fish
could have been a genuine cause of the Hum,

00:04:27.779 --> 00:04:31.849
but the other potential causes have mostly
been disproven.

00:04:31.849 --> 00:04:38.389
However new research has suggested that microseismic
activity from ocean waves impacting the sea

00:04:38.389 --> 00:04:45.419
bed causes our planet itself to vibrate in
certain areas around the globe, causing a

00:04:45.419 --> 00:04:48.580
low-frequency droning sound.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:52.710
Researchers say that this sound is such a
low frequency that only a small percentage

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:55.460
of the population would be able to hear it.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:05:00.979
This ocean-based answer also explains why
the Hum is more commonly heard in costal towns.

00:05:00.979 --> 00:05:06.139
So for some this answer has finally settled
their life-long quest to locate the source

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:09.050
of their annoying, ear-penetrating friend.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:30.229
But for other Hum sufferers who disbelieve
this explanation, their search continues.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:35.490
Thanks for watching.

